cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: "# Date Values & Formats in Oracle\r

      - **DATE** is the main datatype used in Oracle for storing date values\r

      - oracle databases stores the date values in internal numeric format\r

      - it stores a seven-byte number that contains the century, year, month,
      day, and hour, minute, and second\r

      - there are many different date representations in Oracle like
      ('DD-MON-RR', 'DD-MM-YY', 'DD/MM/YYYY', etc)\r

      \r

      | CENTURY | YEAR | MONTH | DAY | HOUR | MINUTE | SECOND |\r

      | ------- | ---- | ----- | --- | ---- | ------ | ------ |\r

      | 19      | 03   | 06    | 17  | 17   | 10     | 43     |\r

      \r

      \  - DD=day\r

      \  - MON=month\r

      \  - RR=allows use to show 20th-century dates in the 21st century using
      only **two** digits; converts two digit years into four digit years by
      rounding\r

      \  - YYYY=full digit year\r

      \  - YY=last two digits of the year"
    languageId: markdown
